I am writing to request information under the FOI Act.
Could you please provide me with the following information:
•	The number of applications received for Housing Adaptation Grants (the Housing Adaptation Grant for People with a Disability; the Mobility Aids Grant; and the Housing Aid for Older People Grant) from 1 January 2023 to 1 August 2023;
•	The number of grants awarded for Housing Adaptation Grants (the Housing Adaptation Grant for People with a Disability; the Mobility Aids Grant; and the Housing Aid for Older People Grant) from 1 January 2023 to 1 August 2023;
•	The value (in euros €) of grants awarded for Housing Adaptation Grants (the Housing Adaptation Grant for People with a Disability; the Mobility Aids Grant; and the Housing Aid for Older People Grant) from 1 January 2023 to 1 August 2023;
•	The number of people on the waiting list for Housing Adaptation Grants (the Housing Adaptation Grant for People with a Disability; the Mobility Aids Grant; and the Housing Aid for Older People Grant) as of 1st August 2023;
•	The number of grant applications for Housing Adaptation Grants (the Housing Adaptation Grant for People with a Disability; the Mobility Aids Grant; and the Housing Aid for Older People Grant) from 1 January 2023 to 1 August 2023 which were denied

Can you please provide all records relating to planning enforcement case Ref: S9072 and related processes, including but not limited to:
all work and communication records relating to the case;
the procedure guides, training materials, internal KPIs and governance controls used in enforcement decisions

Under the Freedom of Information Act, I wish to request the following in relation to all active quarry sites operating in the council's administrative area which have planning permission (or an expired planning permission):
•	The most up-to-date list of all active quarries with active planning permission;
•	The most up-to-date list of all active quarries with expired planning permission;
•	For each quarry, a copy of the record (be it invoice, receipt, council letter, etc) confirming receipt/lodging of a Restoration Bond / surety bond (financial details can be redacted as required) as required as per planning conditions to ensure satisfactory reinstatement of the site following the completion of extraction, or to pay a contribution towards the cost of upgrading or repairing the local road network

1.	To ask SDCC for a copy of all correspondence by 'The Studio Cafe' in Rathfarnham Village, Dublin 14 requesting the annex of 3No. carpark spaces outside the premises to be used for a customer seating area;
2.	To request confirmation if any additional council rates are payable for the use of these car park spaces as retail premises;
3.	To request copy of approvals or relevent exemptions from planning permission guidelines;
4.	To request copy of health and safety, traffic management, risk assessment and method statements, or other documentation on file and available in relation to said annex;
5.	To ask the Council for clarification on the competition requirement that other trading outlets who offer similar services (cafe, food, coffees etc.) be allowed to tender for those or any other village parking spaces to be available in the same way.

I am requesting any and all records since 1 July 2022 to date, which relate to: 
•	Decisions relating to the cataloguing and/or categorising of all Young Adult non-fiction books, including any re-categorisation of such books from Young Adult to Adult; 
•	Any changes which have been made to such cataloguing procedures, and the decision-making process preceding any such changes;
•	The process by which readers / library members are permitted to advance to Young Adult borrowing categories (aged 12-14 years and 15-17 years, respectively); 
•	The Data Protection Impact Assessment(s) carried out in relation to any requirement which has been implemented by the Library, whereby staff must obtain written consent from parents before young readers are permitted to be moved up to Young Adult category of borrower (whether in the 12-14 years category or the 15-17 years category).

The requested records are to include, but not be limited to: 
•	Meeting minutes, memos, diary entries; 
•	Documents, drafts, policies, guidelines, operating procedures, job aids; 
•	Letters, emails, both internal and to/from external sources.

Could we please request the following under the Freedom of Information Act 2014:

Euthanasia Statistics
1.	How many dogs were euthanised in 2021, 2022, 2023 and to date in 2024;
2.	Please provide a breakdown of breed and rationale for all dogs euthanised;
3.	Please confirm if efforts were made to reunite these dogs with owners (where they were found straying) or to rehome them (in all instances).
4.	Please provide a copy of the euthanasia policy utilised by the pound. If there is no such policy, please provide information as to how decisions are made re euthanasia and who is responsible for making the decision. 
Aggressive Behaviour / Dog Attack Statistics
1.	The Control of Dogs Statistics note that statistics on aggressive behaviour / dog attacks have been compiled by local authorities. Please provide a copy of these statistics for 2022, 2023 and to date in 2024. We obviously do not need personal details but would like to understand: 
a.	How many incidences of aggression / dog attacks there were in total;
b.	A breakdown by category of type of incident / attack if available;
c.	Breed(s) involved;
d.	If dogs entered the pound as a result of such incidence / attack (whether by way of straying, surrender or seizure); and
e.	If these dogs entering the pound were euthanised as a result.
XL Bully Ban Implementation
1.	Copies of all materials / information / guidance provided to all dog wardens in relation to the XL Bully Ban;
2.	Confirmation as to what training was provided to dog wardens in relation to the XL Bully Ban and copies of all materials / information / guidance provided to dog wardens as part of any training in respect of the XL Bully Ban. 
We understand training took place over 3 days (2 in September and 1 in October) – is this correct? Was this part of a standard training programme or additional training given? 
3.	How many dog wardens are in your local authority and conformation as to whether all dog wardens attended all training days in respect of the XL Bully Ban and, if not, confirm which wardens have not undertaken the training. 
4.	Confirmation as to whether any other local authority staff have received training or information in respect of the XL Bully Ban and, if so, what categories of staff. Please also provide copies of all materials / information / guidance provided to such staff.

